     1	# Memory
     2	A convenience tool for memories stored in the memory directory (`$MEMORY_DIR`) that automatically commits changes. The harness pushes clean committed memory changes after the turn for remote MemFS agents.
     3	
     4	Files stored inside of `system/` eventually become part of the agent's system prompt, so are always in the context window and do not need to be re-read. Other files only have metadata in the system prompt, so may need to be explicitly read to be updated. 
     5	
     6	Supported operations on memory files:  
     7	- `str_replace`
     8	- `insert`
     9	- `delete` (files, or directories recursively)
    10	- `rename` (path rename only)
    11	- `update_description`
    12	- `create`
    13	For larger reorganizations, edit the projected files directly and commit the changes yourself (see the syncing instructions in your system prompt).
    14	
    15	Path formats accepted:
    16	- relative memory file paths (e.g. `system/contacts.md`, `reference/project/team.md`)
    17	- absolute paths only when they are inside `$MEMORY_DIR`
    18	
    19	Note: absolute paths outside `$MEMORY_DIR` are rejected.
    20	
    21	When creating or deleting files, check for `[[path]]` references in other memory files that may need to be added or updated. Keeping references consistent ensures future discoverability.
    22	
    23	Examples:
    24	
    25	```python
    26	# Replace text in a memory file 
    27	memory(command="str_replace", reason="Update theme preference", file_path="system/human/preferences.md", old_string="theme: dark", new_string="theme: light")
    28	
    29	# Insert text at line 5
    30	memory(command="insert", reason="Add note about meeting", file_path="reference/history/meeting-notes.md", insert_line=5, insert_text="New note here")
    31	
    32	# Delete a memory file 
    33	memory(command="delete", reason="Remove stale notes", file_path="reference/history/old_notes.md")
    34	
    35	# Rename a memory file 
    36	memory(command="rename", reason="Promote temp notes", old_path="reference/history/temp.md", new_path="reference/history/permanent.md")
    37	
    38	# Update a block description
    39	memory(command="update_description", reason="Clarify coding prefs block", file_path="system/human/prefs/coding.md", description="The user's coding preferences.")
    40	
    41	# Create a block with starting text
    42	memory(command="create", reason="Track coding preferences", file_path="system/human/prefs/coding.md", description="The user's coding preferences.", file_text="The user seems to add type hints to all of their Python code.")
    43	
    44	# Create an empty block
    45	memory(command="create", reason="Create coding preferences block", file_path="reference/history/coding_preferences.md", description="The user's coding preferences.")
    46	```
     1	Apply a codex-style patch to memory files in `$MEMORY_DIR`, then automatically commit the change. The harness pushes clean committed memory changes after the turn for remote MemFS agents.
     2	
     3	This is similar to `apply_patch`, but scoped to the memory filesystem and with memory-aware guardrails.
     4	
     5	- Required args:
     6	  - `reason` — git commit message for the memory change
     7	  - `input` — patch text using the standard apply_patch format
     8	
     9	Patch format:
    10	- `*** Begin Patch`
    11	- `*** Add File: <path>`
    12	- `*** Update File: <path>`
    13	  - optional `*** Move to: <path>`
    14	  - one or more `@@` hunks with ` `, `-`, `+` lines
    15	- `*** Delete File: <path>`
    16	- `*** End Patch`
    17	
    18	Path rules:
    19	- Relative paths are interpreted inside memory repo
    20	- Absolute paths are allowed only when under `$MEMORY_DIR`
    21	- Paths outside memory repo are rejected
    22	
    23	Memory rules:
    24	- Operates on markdown memory files (`.md`)
    25	- Updated/deleted files must be valid memory files with frontmatter
    26	- `read_only: true` files cannot be modified
    27	- If adding a file without frontmatter, frontmatter is created automatically
    28	
    29	Git behavior:
    30	- Stages changed memory paths
    31	- Commits with `reason`
    32	- Uses agent identity author (`<agent_id>@letta.com`)
    33	- Remote MemFS push is handled by the harness after the turn
    34	
    35	Example:
    36	```python
    37	memory_apply_patch(
    38	  reason="Refine coding preferences",
    39	  input="""*** Begin Patch
    40	*** Update File: system/human/prefs/coding.md
    41	@@
    42	-Use broad abstractions
    43	+Prefer small focused helpers
    44	*** End Patch"""
    45	)
    46	```
